        abstract:
          "It is commonly known that many traditional activities are performed in Northern Nigeria using horses for entertainment and for maintaining traditions known to the people of the region. Durbar and Hawan Sallah are among the things that facilitate observance of such traditions, through the use of horses as main instruments entertain gatherings for generations. In Northern Nigeria, Durbar and Hawan Sallah have been performed by many people in several areas since pre-colonial period, but the modern Durbar and Hawan Sallah developed from the time of British administrators who introduced and encouraged them in their entertainment activities. The main of the objective of thisstudy is to discuss the role of Durbar and Hawan Sallah in sustaining old traditions in Northern Nigeria. Qualitative method of research was used in collecting data through the use of primary, secondary and tertiary sources. The study discovered that horses play a vital role in maintaining the Hausa culture in Northern Nigeria during celebrations of annual Sallah festivities or during an important occasions. Keywords: Durbar, Horse, Tradition, Hawan Sallah, Entertainment.",
