        abstract:
          "This study assesses the role of religious identities in weakening the Nigeria's democracy, progress and unity. The multi-religious nature of the Nigerian society has continued to remain a challenge to good governance, economic advancement and even the survival of the country as a united and indivisible country. These religious divisions and lack of religious tolerance continue to challenge the development of the country since its return to democratic rule after prolonged military rule and since its independence from a colonial rule. These divisions along religious lines sometimes end up in to conflict between the followers of these religions in the country causing loss of lives and property, damaging government and individual properties thereby drawing the progress of the country backward. Keywords: Religion, Identities, Democracy, Unity, Development, Rule, Good governance and Progress.",
